{#- The hill backdrop: three silhouettes cut from one drawing, written by
    tools/gen-hills.py into hill-1/2/3.svg, and the torii gate standing on
    the near one. Decorative only, hence aria-hidden — the page says nothing
    that these carry.

    Back to front, so the near hill paints over everything behind it. The
    three hills share one viewBox, so they need no offsets of their own: the
    stylesheet places the box and every hill lands where it belongs inside
    it. The gate is not one of them — it is a bounded object with a box of
    its own, which is why it carries no `hill` class and does not pick up
    their placement rule.

    Its ORDER here is the whole of how it stands on the hill: after hills 3
    and 2 so it is in front of both, before hill 1 so the near hill paints
    over its feet. Move that line and the gate either floats or disappears.

    Dropping any of these is a matter of deleting its line, which is how
    this is meant to be reused at the foot of an inner page. #}
<div class="hills" aria-hidden="true">
  <span class="hill hill-3"></span>
  <span class="hill hill-2"></span>
  <span class="torii"></span>
  <span class="hill hill-1"></span>
</div>
